{"id": "tech-3", "headline": "Ladybird browser alpha opens for testing", "source": "The Verge", "url": "https://www.theverge.com/tech/1040872/ladybird-indie-browser-engine-alpha-testing", "published": "2026-11-23", "url_verified": true, "pages": ["Ladybird, an independent web browser with an engine built from scratch, launched in alpha on macOS and Linux on Monday. Developer Andreas Kling announced the release after more than four years of work. Most popular browsers rely on one of three engines: Gecko, WebKit or Blink. Ladybird is backed by a nonprofit that aims for an independent, fast and secure browser that respects privacy. Its code began in C++, and developers have been porting parts to Rust with the help of AI. Kling called the browser modest but functional and warned that some websites will not work. A Windows version is planned for a later stage. Source: The Verge."], "qr": {"n": 37, "rows": ["1111111000101111001110010010001111111", "1000001010100111101011001011001000001", "1011101000001101000011100001001011101", "1011101011101011010100101101101011101", "1011101001000001111101010010001011101", "1000001011011000000011101001101000001", "1111111010101010101010101010101111111", "0000000001110010101011110001000000000", "1111101111010000110000011101110101010", "1011100110101111000110010110000101110", "1111111101100111101001100001111011101", "0001110000101101001111101000110001010", "0100011000001011010100111100011111101", "0110110111100001111111010010000100110", "0000011010011000001010000111011100111", "0011110010010010101001000011011101001", "0011001011110000010100111100001011101", "0001010101001111001111111010100100110", "0100101011000111001010001101110010111", "0000010100001101000111000000000100001", "1011111001101011011000101101011110111", "0111000011000001011110010100100100010", "0111011010111001100000101111101100111", "0001110000110010100111111011110100001", "1101101100010001010100100111011010111", "1101000111001110100111110100100100010", "101010101110011100